    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d520">

                <pb facs="0659" n="547" xml:id="pg547"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.515/431a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-03-02T14:00:00-05:00">March 2, 1935—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>63. Press stories now show that there are in process international diplomatic
                    conversations on the subject of the situation in the Far East, especially China,
                    and the possibility of cooperative financial assistance to China.</p>
                <p>A variety of initiatives, from China, from Japan and from Great Britain has
                    brought about this development. The British Government has apparently elected to
                    constitute itself the prime mover in the canvassing of the powers with regard to
                    possibilities. Department will give you details as soon as expedient and
                    possible.</p>
                <p>Meanwhile, Department suggests that you avoid being drawn into discussion of the
                    subject, stating merely, to possible inquirers, that the question, whatever it
                    is, is being handled between the various foreign offices interested and
                    concerned.</p>
                <p>Repeat to Tokyo [as] No. 30.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
